dit Known Hosts (SSH) security artifacts by uploading files from your local system.  See: Manage Security for Edge Integration Cell\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-14\nValid as Of: 2025-09-14\nVersion: 2507\n\n--- Record 114 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Updates on Component Monitor\nDescription:   The Component Monitor page has been redesigned.  There's a new Auditlog Agent component available.  Selected metrics are now displayed for certain components.    See: Component Monitor\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-14\nValid as Of: 2025-09-14\nVersion: 2507\n\n--- Record 115 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: XML Threat Protection Policy\nDescription: The XML Threat Protection policy has been introduced to safeguard XML-based applications and APIs from malicious attacks. This policy enforces strict rules on XML data to prevent common threats such as recursive payloads, excessive node depth, and oversized payloads.   See, XML Threat Protection Policy.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-14\nValid as Of: 2025-09-14\nVersion: 2507\n\n--- Record 116 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Project assistant capabilities for SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition in Enterprise Portfolio and Project Management, to read the due or overdue activities in a Project, WBS Element, Network\nDescription: The following transactional project assistant capabilities are now supported in Enterprise Portfolio and Project Management for SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition.    Display due or overdue activities in a Project  Display due or overdue activities in a WBS Element  Display due or overdue activities in a Network    For more information, see Read Due or Overdue Activities in Project, WBS Element, Network.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-31\nValid as Of: 2025-09-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 117 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support Extended for Mass Change of Sales Orders\nDescription: Joule capabilities in Sales for Mass Change of Sales Orders are now also supported in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition 2022.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-21\nValid as Of: 2025-09-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 118 ---\nComponent: Decentralized Identity Verification\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Adaptaton of DCP Credential Offer API to RC4 specifications\nDescription: Decentralized Identity Verification is now compliant with the RC4 release candidate specifications for the DCP credential issuance flow.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-09-11\nVersion: 3.13\n\n--- Record 119 ---\nComponent: Decentralized Identity Verification\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Addition of Credential Creation UI Form\nDescription: You can now enter credential data through a UI form before issuing the credential.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-09-11\nVersion: 3.13\n\n--- Record 120 ---\nComponent: Decentralized Identity Verification\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Possibility to Add Custom Context to DID Document\nDescription: You can now extend the DID Document by adding a custom context.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-09-11\nVersion: 3.13\n\n", "--- Record 2621 ---\nComponent: Cloud Portal Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support Update Operation in Identity Provisioning Transformation\nDescription: The default target transformation code of SAP Cloud Portal system in the Identity Provisioning service, has been enhanced to also support updates to existing user records. With this enhancement, when a user attribute changes (for example email address or Global ID) the record is updated instead of being skipped.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-11\nValid as Of: 2024-07-11\nVersion: 2406B\n\n--- Record 2622 ---\nComponent: Connectivity\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Java Connector 3.1.10.0 - Bug Fixes\nDescription: Release of Java Connector (JCo) version 3.1.10.0 provides the following bug fixes:      If a remote-enabled function module (RFM) has multiple TABLES parameters, the content of one or more received JCoTable objects could have been incorrect, all rows of affected tables being only partly filled.   In this case, each row was populated with data only up to a certain column and following fields were empty or contained their type-specific initial value. The full content of the first TABLES parameter was always correct.   This program error occurred under special complex preconditions, for which the affected TABLES parameters needed to have a certain layout structure of field types, while the affected table content was being transferred in compressed row-based serialization format.    Note  This was a regression bug which had been introduced with JCo 3.1.9.0        Changed values of property jco.destination.repository_destination, which were returned from the currently active DestinationDataProvider instance for a given destination name, were not processed correctly by the JCo runtime, and already existing JCoDestination instances for that destination name were not updated with the new value.   Such existing JCoDestination instances still returned the old JCoRepository instance, although a different one might be associated with the newly configured repository destination.      These issues have been fixed.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-11\nValid as Of: 2024-07-11\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2623 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Joule Booster\nDescription: You can now select SAP SuccessFactors system in the Select Integrations screen of the Joule booster instead of manually typing the tenant URL and the company code. You need to ensure that you have registered the system in SAP BTP under  System Landscape before you run the booster.  Note  Joule will continue to work seamlessly for existing integrations and no actions are required for the set up done before this change.  See Register an SAP SuccessFactors System in a Global Account in SAP BTP and Integration with SAP SuccessFactors. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-11\nValid as Of: 2024-07-11\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2624 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 40.17.0\nDescription: Cloud Foundry has been updated from 40.12.0 to 40.17.0.  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v40.17.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v40.16.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v40.15.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v40.14.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v40.13.0  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-11\nValid as Of: 2024-07-11\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2625 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Display Card Header in Wizard\nDescription: For cards that were added to a custom wizard, it's possible to choose whether to display the card header in the wizard. This feature is not applicable to cards that are not part of a wizard.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-11\nValid as Of: 2024-07-11\nVersion: 2406B\n\n--- Record 2626 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: External User Access to Sub-Workspaces\nDescription: The option to enable external user access to sub-workspace will be blocked when the parent workspace is not accessible to external users.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-11\nValid as Of: 2024-07-11\nVersion: 2406B\n\n--- Record 2627 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: HTML5 Business Solution as a Content Provider\nDescription: It is now possible to create an HTML5 business solution that behaves as a content provider in the subaccount.  The HTML5 business solution can be consumed by the local subaccount and also by remote subaccounts that access it via destinations.  To configure", "2024-07-11\nVersion: 2406B\n\n--- Record 2627 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: HTML5 Business Solution as a Content Provider\nDescription: It is now possible to create an HTML5 business solution that behaves as a content provider in the subaccount.  The HTML5 business solution can be consumed by the local subaccount and also by remote subaccounts that access it via destinations.  To configure an HTML5 business solution as a content provider, the following actions are required:   Provider subaccount: the HTML5 code should be adjusted and include a cdm.json file that defines the design-time business content (for example, roles, groups, spaces & pages), and destinations.    Consumer subaccount: it is required to configure destinations that will point to the HTML5 business solution and create the content provider.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-11\nValid as Of: 2024-07-11\nVersion: 2406B\n\n--- Record 2628 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support Update Operation in Identity Provisioning Transformation\nDescription: The default target transformation code of an SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition system in the Identity Provisioning service, has been enhanced to also support updates to existing user records. With this enhancement, when a user attribute changes (for example email address or Global ID), the record is updated instead of being skipped.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-11\nValid as Of: 2024-07-11\nVersion: 2406B\n\n--- Record 2629 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Updated Dev Guide for Card Interaction\nDescription: The Developer Guide for card interaction has been enhanced. Developers can now find sample cards with explanations in Github. For more information, see Configuring Interaction Between Cards.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-11\nValid as Of: 2024-07-11\nVersion: 2406B\n\n--- Record 2630 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: What's New Information Added to SAP Companion\nDescription: To display What's New information in the in-app help of a site, you need to change the value of the version parameter from Cloud to latest in the SAP Companion configuration in the Site Settings.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-11\nValid as Of: 2024-07-11\nVersion: 2406B\n\n", "--- Record 2811 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Managing Groups\nDescription: You can use the Application Name field in the filter bar for advanced search. See List and Edit Groups.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-05\nValid as Of: 2024-06-05\nVersion: 26181\n\n--- Record 2812 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Real-time logs show the origin of the users\nDescription: Real-time logs have been improved. They now show the origin of the users that have been created, updated, or deleted in the SAP BTP XS Advanced UAA (Cloud Foundry) target system.  See: Monitor Real-Time Logs.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-05\nValid as Of: 2024-06-05\nVersion: 26181\n\n--- Record 2813 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-05\nValid as Of: 2024-06-05\nVersion: 26181\n\n--- Record 2814 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: SAP Market Communication for Utilities - bundle option documentation\nDescription: Documentation for SAP Market Communication for Utilities bundle option is now available.  See: SAP Market Communication for Utilities Bundle\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-05\nValid as Of: 2024-06-05\nVersion: 26181\n\n--- Record 2815 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: User update capability for SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nDescription: Identity Provisioning now supports update operation for existing users in SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition target and proxy systems. Up to now users could only be created and deleted in the SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition systems.  See:    SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition (Target)      SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition (Proxy)    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-05\nValid as Of: 2024-06-05\nVersion: 26181\n\n--- Record 2816 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: SAP Market Communication for Utilities - bundle option documentation\nDescription: Documentation for SAP Market Communication for Utilities bundle option is now available.  For more information, see: SAP Market Communication for Utilities Bundle\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-05\nValid as Of: 2024-06-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2817 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: User update capability for SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nDescription: Identity Provisioning now supports update operation for existing users in SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition target and proxy systems. Up to now users could only be created and deleted in the SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition systems.  For more information, see:    SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition (Target)      SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition (Proxy)    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-05\nValid as Of: 2024-06-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2818 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Normalized Rate – Treatment of Item Quantity Zero\nDescription: The normalized condition rate, which is the condition rate converted into the sales unit of measure and the document currency, cannot be calculated for 